## Primary Sources

1. Heuer, Richards J. Jr. (1999). *Psychology of Intelligence Analysis*. Center for
the Study of Intelligence, Central Intelligence Agency. The foundational text on
ACH and cognitive bias in intelligence analysis.

2. CIA (2009). *A Tradecraft Primer: Structured Analytic Techniques for Improving
Intelligence Analysis*. CIA Center for the Study of Intelligence. Covers ACH,
Key Assumptions Check, Devil's Advocacy, and Deception Detection.

3. Mandel, D.R. & Barnes, A. (2019). "The 'analysis of competing hypotheses' in
intelligence analysis." *Applied Cognitive Psychology*. Empirical study of 50
intelligence analysts finding ACH increased transparency but did not significantly
improve accuracy over unstructured analysis.

4. Pherson, K.H. & Pherson, R.H. (2016). *Critical Thinking for Strategic
Intelligence*, 2nd ed. CQ Press. Comprehensive structured analytic techniques
reference with CI-specific applications.

5. CIA v. Sims, 471 U.S. 159 (1985). US Supreme Court case establishing mosaic
theory in national security law — individual unclassified information fragments
can collectively reveal classified conclusions.

6. Prunckun, H. (2019). *Counterintelligence Theory and Practice*, 2nd ed.
Rowman & Littlefield. Operational CI frameworks including dangle analysis,
counter-espionage investigation, and deception campaign design.

7. ODNI (2015). *Intelligence Community Directive 203: Analytic Standards*.
Establishes the nine analytic standards including structured analytic techniques
requirement for IC products.

8. Johnson, L.K. (2017). *National Security Intelligence*, 2nd ed. Polity Press.
Comprehensive overview of CI structures, Five Eyes alliance CI operations, and
intelligence cycle dynamics.

9. NCSC (2024). *National Counterintelligence Strategy of the United States of
America*. National Counterintelligence and Security Center, ODNI. Three-pillar
strategy for countering gray-zone FIE threats, safeguarding strategic advantages,
and building future CI operational foundations.

10. ODNI (2024). *IC OSINT Strategy 2024-2026*. Office of the Director of
National Intelligence. Four-pillar strategy for professionalizing and integrating
OSINT capabilities across the Intelligence Community.

11. Kraven Security (2026). "Structured Analytic Techniques: How to Analyze
Threat Intelligence." Comprehensive SAT taxonomy covering six technique families
with CI-applicable deception detection, key assumptions check, argument mapping,
and indicator generation frameworks.

12. Pherson, R.H. & Heuer, R.J. Jr. (2020). *Structured Analytic Techniques for
Intelligence Analysis*, 3rd ed. CQ Press. The definitive SAT reference with 66
techniques across eight families, including CI-specific deception detection and
structured CI analysis methods.

